<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marias Massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marias Massacre was an attack by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army on a camp of Piegan Blackfeet on the Marias River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a> on 23 January 1870. Troops under Major Eugene Baker struck the peaceful band of Heavy Runner and killed well over a hundred people, most of them women, children and old men. The killings caused a public outcry and contributed to the transfer of Indian affairs away from army control.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Marias Massacre</b> was part of the Indian Wars.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-23">23 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The Blackfoot had signed the Lame Bull Treaty with the United States in 1855; weakened by the <b>Marias Massacre</b> of 1870 and the near extinction of the bison, they signed Treaty 7 with Canada in 1877, negotiated by Crowfoot.</blockquote><a href="/state/blackfoot-confederacy">Blackfoot Confederacy</a></li></ul></section>
